		     paired with its own decorative font, matching how Aeon Nox 5 pairs entrance style with
		     typeface, not just motion. tween="elastic" easing="out" gives a genuine bounce-and-settle,
		     not a flat linear move - confirmed live to actually render (an earlier from-scratch
		     attempt looked like it never animated at all; root cause was that font_culrc_current from
		     our own bundled Font.xml never loads - Kodi's WindowXMLDialog does not support a custom
		     addon-bundled Font.xml at all, confirmed via repeated debug-log inspection - so all text
		     was silently rendering at a tiny skin-fallback size, making the motion/rotation only a
		     couple of pixels and invisible). The decorative fonts here (culrc_exo2/_ranchers/
		     _luckiestguy) come from lib/fontinstall.py, which patches them directly into the active
		     skin's own Font.xml (same technique script.xderecx.aeonnox5lyricsfix uses for Aeon Nox 5,
		     generalized to any writable-storage skin) - run once from Settings > Current-line display.
		     Until that's run (or on a read-only-storage skin, e.g. the OS-bundled default on some
		     builds), these font names simply don't resolve and Kodi falls back to its own default -
		     not a crash, just no decorative look yet. part4 (rest of the line) and the translation
		     block intentionally keep using plain always-available skin fonts (font37/font20), not
		     the decorative ones, since that text is secondary. Each word also gets its own small
		     fixed rotation (per-part-number static tilt) for the scattered/thrown-on-screen look.
